<p>The producer's <a href="${source.teachers}">whisky-range page</a> names Ardmore's peated single malt and describes Highland Cream with malt, fruit and honey alongside smoke. An ingredient in a blend can be a single malt without making the finished blend itself a single malt. The category is still blended Scotch, which is why a distillery name and a bottle's category should be read as different pieces of information.</p>
